# Publish after every modification

Whenever you change project files (HTML, CSS, JS, assets, copy, config), finish the turn by committing and pushing to `origin` on the current branch.

- Do this even if the user did not say "commit", "push", or "pubblica".
- Use the standard git commit protocol (status, diff, log, HEREDOC message, status after).
- Never force-push unless the user explicitly asks.
- Never commit secrets (`.env`, credentials, keys).
- If there is nothing to commit, skip quietly.
- Prefer one commit per coherent batch of changes in the turn.
